Open defects: `world/game-developer`#7 (low): end screen can be skipped instantly by a click/key right at match end, so the winner can go unseen. Cosmetic notes in the same issue (blinking play-again prompt, attract-mode ball over title text).

Difficulty observation (not filed, judged against brief priority 2): against a reactive bot with 150-250 ms latency the computer wins 5-0/5-1; against a bot that predicts the ball's intercept with 120 ms latency the player won 5-0 in all 6 matches (CPU scored 0 points). Beatable, and the computer scores against weak play; it does not score against a precise player. Producer/game-developer may tune CPU_SPEED/aim error if "computer also wins points" must hold against strong players.

